  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1180",
      "html": "<p>Duopalatinus peruanus Eigenmann &amp; Allen, 1942. Family Pimelodidae. Type locality: Río Puinagua, mouth of Río Pacaya, Río Ucayali system, Peru. Etymology: Latin Duo = two + palatum = roof of the mouth. IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/pimelodidae/duopalatinus_peruanus.htm",
      "html": "<ul><li>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (LC)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1180",
      "html": "<p>South America: Amazon and Orinoco River basins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/pimelodidae/duopalatinus_peruanus.htm",
      "html": "<p>South America: Amazon and Orinoco River basins. Type locality: Rio Puinagua, mouth of Rio Pacaya [Río Ucayali system, Peru].</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/pimelodidae/duopalatinus_peruanus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Present in the Orthon sub-basin (Amazon Basin). Also recorded in the Madre de Dios and Beni sub-basins (Amazon Basin) (Torrico et al. 2020).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1180",
      "html": "<p>Breeding: unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1180",
      "html": "<p>Maximum size 150 mm (5.9\") SL.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/pimelodidae/duopalatinus_peruanus.htm",
      "html": "<p>There are two species in this genus, D. peruanus and D. emarginatus. Duopalatinus is classified under the \"Calophysus-Pimelodus clade\". Within this clade, it is considered a part of the \"Pimelodus-group\" of Pimelodids, which also includes Pimelodus, Exallodontus, Cheirocerus, Iheringichthys, Bergiaria, Bagropsis, Parapimelodus, Platysilurus, Platystomatichthys, and Propimelodus.</p><p>Colouration: Body and head pale grey, with the dorsal region slightly darker. Ventral region whitish. Adipose fin pale grey; all other fins yellowish.</p><p>Etymology: The specific name peruanus means belonging to Peru.</p><p>Despite the little information available on this species, it has a wide range and no apparent threats. Therefore, it is assessed as Least Concern (LC) (IUCN 2024).</p>"
    },
    {
